ZTEXT0010000108b99de9b0a0000000
Zero file operations 0.12

All implementations and product tests in this directory are original Zero.
compiler.zero contains the canonical executable definitions. The .zero.part
files are source fragments, not scripts or assembler input. author.zero resolves
original byte-encoding labels without an assembler or external compiler.

Expression API:
  :create[path]                     0 success, -1 failure
  :del[path]                        0 success, -1 failure
  :readfile[path|buffer|capacity]    bytes read, -1 failure
  :save[path|buffer|length]          bytes saved, -1 failure
  :writefile[path|buffer|length]     bytes written, -1 failure
  :watch[root|buffer|capacity]       listing bytes, -1 failure
  :search[pattern|buffer|capacity]   listing bytes, -1 failure
  :go[root]                         0 success, -1 failure
  :disks[buffer|capacity]           root-list bytes, -1 failure

Paths are NUL-terminated. Buffers and their capacity are caller-owned.
The low-level API accepts text or binary file content without transformation.
Native whole-file and listing buffers are limited to 65536 bytes.
create preserves an existing readable regular file, or creates an empty file.
del requires an existing regular file. Final symlinks and Windows reparse points
are refused. Directory operations remain separate existing primitives.
save creates or truncates; writefile creates exclusively and refuses overwrite.
Native successful writes flush and close. save is not an atomic replacement:
a write/flush/close error can leave a truncated or partial existing file.
Exclusive writefile attempts to remove its own newly created file after error.
readfile reads the observed size and checks EOF, refusing growth/shrink or
insufficient capacity. It does not claim a snapshot against concurrent writers.

watch and search return regular-file names, each terminated by one NUL. The
byte count includes these terminators, with no additional list terminator.
An empty list returns zero. Enumeration order follows the filesystem and is not
promised to be alphabetical. Overflow returns -1; any partial buffer is invalid.
Ezero converts successful results into one-based text lists and validates UTF-8.
watch("") lists the current root/directory. search("") lists all current files.
search splits only the final path component into a pattern. A trailing separator
means all names in that directory. Without wildcards the match is exact.
The original matcher is case-sensitive on every target: * consumes zero or more
characters and ? consumes one UTF-8 scalar. No recursive search is implied.
Native path separators use host syntax; guest paths use A:|name.

Native go changes the process working directory. Native disks exposes logical
roots: Linux returns /, Windows returns available drive letters. Linux / is not
an inventory of physical disks. Guest disks exposes the system's volume roots.

Guest calls use the optional ZEROFS01 descriptor at app context offset184.
Missing descriptor or incompatible version returns -1 without switching.
Descriptor fields are 64-bit values:
  0 magic0x313053464f52455a; 8 version1; 16 service continuation;
  24 app continuation; 32 operation; 40 path; 48 buffer; 56 count;
  64 result; 72 driver status; 80 phase; 88 reserved; 96..255 kernel-private.
Operation IDs: 1readfile, 2save, 3writefile, 4create, 5del, 6watch,
7search, 8go, 9disks. Caller publishes phase1 and result-1, switches, then
requires phase2 before reading the result. This shared-memory cooperative ABI
is not a process-isolation boundary. The kernel applies guest filesystem limits.

AMD64 continuation version1 already records arena bounds. IA32 raw continuations
retain version1, a 64KiB arena, and frame fields0/4/8/12. IA32 applications use
version2, a 4MiB arena, and frame fields32/36/40/44. The kernel restore validates
both versions with their respective geometry. No old kernel receives the new
service descriptor. Ordinary compiler/frontend applications receive no service.

Compiler output capacity is524288 bytes. Subsequent arena buffers are shifted
by32768 bytes; total compiler reservation4055648 remains within its4MiB arena.
Guest bundle compiler slot remains159744 bytes; the builder must reject overflow.
